\contentsline {section}{: Has the most complete licensing — popular artists like Jay Chou and Mayday are basically only on QQ Music. The sound quality options are also very rich, and members can enable lossless quality. If you care about “being able to find every song you want to listen to”, QQ Music is the most reliable choice.}{97}{section*.29}%
\contentsline {section}{: Built into iPhone, no need to download an additional app. Best integration with CarPlay, very convenient when driving.}{98}{section*.29}%
\contentsline {section}{: If you want a more refined experience, this paid app is worth buying. Nice interface, smooth gesture controls — swipe up and down on the left to adjust brightness, on the right to adjust volume, swipe left and right to fast-forward and rewind. Supports DTS and Dolby audio, giving a much stronger immersive feel when watching blockbusters.}{98}{section*.29}%
\contentsline {section}{: If you have a Kindle device, the phone Kindle app can sync your reading progress. Genuine Kindle e-books have much better layout quality than pirated PDFs, but the Kindle China store has closed, so you need to switch to an overseas region.}{99}{section*.29}%
\contentsline {section}{: Don't just max everything out. First ensure frame rate (smoothness), then pursue image quality. 60 fps is much smoother than 30 fps, but 120 fps puts a lot of pressure on the phone — mid-range phones shouldn't force it. If you play competitive games (like Honor of Kings or PUBG Mobile), frame rate priority is far more important than image quality — smooth control feel is a hundred times more important than pretty grass textures.}{100}{section*.29}%
