\contentsline {section}{Execution and response}{184}{section*.49}%
\contentsline {section}{AI LLMs (Large Language Models) are AI systems trained on massive amounts of text data that can understand and generate natural language. You can imagine it as a “super scholar” who has read almost all the text on the internet, capable of answering questions, writing articles, translating, programming, and analyzing data.}{184}{Item.281}%
\contentsline {section}{Conversational assistants}{185}{Item.281}%
\contentsline {section}{Underlying principle}{186}{Item.281}%
\contentsline {section}{Many people use AI like using Baidu—typing in a few keywords. But AI is not a search engine; it's a language model that “reads, understands, and then answers.”}{187}{Item.281}%
\contentsline {section}{: Most AI's training data has a cutoff date (such as early 2024); it doesn't know what happened after that.}{192}{Item.286}%
\contentsline {chapter}{Chapter 23: Programming Thinking and Automation Enlightenment}{195}{chapter*.50}%
\contentsline {section}{Automation is essentially the “if... then...” logic chain, the if-else in programming. Once you understand this way of thinking, even if you never write code in your life, your problem-solving organization will be much stronger. Core elements:}{195}{section*.51}%
\contentsline {section}{: Instructions that run automatically based on trigger conditions, without needing you to manually trigger them. For example, “when the phone connects to car Bluetooth, automatically open the Maps App.” Automations are set up under the “Automation” tab, separate from “Shortcuts.”}{196}{Item.292}%
\contentsline {section}{Tasker is universally recognized as the most powerful automation tool on the Android platform, consistently topping the charts. Honestly, its learning curve is a bit steep and the interface isn't pretty, but once you get the hang of it, you'll feel your phone suddenly becomes omnipotent. Tasker's core is also the “trigger task” pattern:}{197}{Item.292}%
\contentsline {section}{Every morning, automatically read today's schedule from the calendar and generate a text message sent to family via WeChat.}{199}{Item.292}%
\contentsline {section}{: In iOS, most triggers under the “Automation” tab require manual confirmation to run (iOS's security mechanism). However, Wi-Fi connection, Bluetooth connection, and alarm stopped triggers can run fully automatically without confirmation.}{199}{Item.292}%
